    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4027" type="person"
                        >Sam</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I am enclosing my report in CHRISTIANITY AND CRISIS on the German situation.<note
                    type="ea">Vgl. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                        type="person">Paul Tillich</rs>: <rs type="work" ref="#tillich__AB6TMN6G">Visit
                            to Germany</rs> (1948).</note> This of course is a very short article.
                    So if you think I should send a larger typewritten report to CHURCH WORLD
                    SERVICE, an acknowledgement for their sending me to <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs>, I shall be glad to
                    do it. If you think the enclosed article does the job I should be grateful if
                    you give it in my name to the office of CHURCH WORLD SERVICE.</p>
                <p>May I add that I fully agreed with your paper in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__554"
                        type="place">Washington</rs> and regretted very much that you could not
                    attend the other meetings. I think the discussion would have been more fruitful
                    if you would ha<supplied>v</supplied>e been present. On Sunday morning I
                    delivered a report on <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place"
                    >Germany</rs>.</p>
                <closer><salute>Cordially yours,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Prof. Paul Tillich</rs>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>encl</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
